# Jira Test issues and CI output

## Creating Test issues in Jira

Edit the table for your instance.

| What | Value |
|------|--------|
| **Project key** | `EPMRPP` |
| **Issue type** | `Test` |
| **Priority** | Set per **Test priority** (below)—**do not** default every Test to **`Major`**. |
| **Label** (mark AI-generated Tests) | `ai-generated` |
| **Test Steps** field (preconditions + steps) | `customfield_19206` |
| **Expected result** field | `customfield_19207` |
| **Test Library** (TM / library scope; UI may show as library) | `customfield_24000` |
| **Folder** (path under library; UI may show as “Folder”) | `customfield_24001` |
| **Test Requirement** (TM link to User Story; API name **Test requirement**) | `customfield_29300` |

**`customfield_29300`** (**Test requirement** / UI **Test Requirement**) is **`jira_search_fields`** with **`keyword`:** `Test requirement`; visible on Tests such as [EPMRPP-115882](https://jiraeu.epam.com/browse/EPMRPP-115882) (unset). Field ids for **`customfield_19206`**, **`customfield_19207`**, **`customfield_24000`**, **`customfield_24001`** were confirmed via **`jira_get_issue`** on sample Tests [EPMRPP-114175](https://jiraeu.epam.com/browse/EPMRPP-114175) and [EPMRPP-114179](https://jiraeu.epam.com/browse/EPMRPP-114179). On [EPMRPP-114175](https://jiraeu.epam.com/browse/EPMRPP-114175), **`customfield_24000`** = `Test Library` and **`customfield_24001`** = `EPMRPP` (project-root folder)—**do not** use **`EPMRPP`** as the **Folder** for **AI-generated** Tests. On AI-generated sample [EPMRPP-114179](https://jiraeu.epam.com/browse/EPMRPP-114179), **`customfield_24000`** = `Test Library` and **`customfield_24001`** = **`AI Generated`** (**Folder** field id **`customfield_24001`**)—see **Test Folder (required)** below.

### Test Folder (required)

- For **AI-generated** Tests, set **`customfield_24001`** (Folder) to the **`AI Generated`** TM option—on **`jiraeu.epam.com`** the option **label** includes a **trailing space** (`**`AI Generated `**`) as on [EPMRPP-115879](https://jiraeu.epam.com/browse/EPMRPP-115879); mirror **`jira_get_issue`** / **`jira_get_field_options`** for your instance. Same idea as [EPMRPP-114179](https://jiraeu.epam.com/browse/EPMRPP-114179) (`labels` include **`ai-generated`**). **Do not** file AI-generated Tests under the **`EPMRPP`** project-root folder only.
- Keep **`customfield_24000`** = **`Test Library`** per project practice (see [EPMRPP-114179](https://jiraeu.epam.com/browse/EPMRPP-114179)) unless your instance requires a different library value.
- If the **`AI Generated`** folder option is missing in Jira Test Management, create it or obtain valid values via **`jira_get_field_options`** for **`customfield_24001`** (**`project_key=EPMRPP`**, **`issue_type=Test`**) before filing Tests.

### Test priority (required)

**Do not** set **`Major`** on **every** generated Test. Choose **`priority`** as a **Senior QA** would: use valid Jira **Test** priority names for your instance (e.g. **Blocker**, **Critical**, **Major**, **Minor**, **Trivial**—**verify** via story/`jira_get_issue` or team norms).

- **Anchor on the User Story:** Use **`jira_get_issue(STORY_KEY)`** **`priority`** as the **baseline** when assigning each Test’s priority (often match the story for **happy-path / primary AC** cases; **not** every case must equal the story—see below).
- **Raise** when the case guards **release-blocking**, **compliance**, **security**, **billing**, **data loss/corruption**, **permissions for sensitive actions**, or **high regression risk** on a core flow—even if the story priority looks lower, if the scenario is “if this fails, we ship a serious bug,” reflect that.
- **Lower** for **secondary** UX, **edge cases** that rarely fire, **cosmetic** or **copy** checks, **nice-to-have** telemetry-only (e.g. GA) cases, or **optional** paths called out as low impact in the story—without under-stating real risk.
- **Vary across tests** in the same story: primary AC vs edge vs permission matrix rows may legitimately differ (e.g. **Critical** for core create flow, **Minor** for a rare error message).
- **On `jira_update_issue`** when refreshing linked Tests, **re-evaluate** **`priority`** if the story priority or scenario mix changed—include **`priority`** in the updated fields (**Sync with existing Jira Tests**).

### MCP create / update (custom fields)

On **`jira_create_issue`** / **`jira_update_issue`** (mcp-atlassian) or equivalent, pass **`customfield_19206`** (Test Steps), **`customfield_19207`** (Expected result), **`customfield_24000`** (Test Library), **`customfield_24001`** (Folder), and **`customfield_29300`** (**Test Requirement** → User Story **`STORY_KEY`**) using the **same value types** Jira returns for a reference Test (**preferred**—e.g. **`jira_get_issue(EPMRPP-114179)`** for Folder / Test Library; **`jira_get_issue(EPMRPP-115858, fields=customfield_29300)`** or any Test with **`"Test requirement"`** set for the requirement value shape). Empty reference for the field on a Test: [EPMRPP-115882](https://jiraeu.epam.com/browse/EPMRPP-115882). If needed, use **`jira_get_field_options`** for **`customfield_24001`** with **`project_key=EPMRPP`** and **`issue_type=Test`** to obtain valid option ids or display strings.

Use these in **`jira_create_issue`** / **`jira_update_issue`** (mcp-atlassian) or equivalent (**`jira_createIssue`** / **`jira_updateIssue`**). **Every** new Test must include the **`ai-generated`** label. Set **`priority`** per **Test priority** above—not a blanket **`Major`** on all issues.

**Create and link** Test issues **only via Jira MCP** (**`jira_create_issue`** / **`jira_update_issue`** and issue links)—**do not** add a separate REST path that **creates** tests or replaces MCP. **GitHub Actions:** after the headless agent finishes, **`scripts/ensure-jira-test-tm-fields.js`** uses Jira REST (**`PUT /rest/api/2/issue/{key}`**) **only** to normalize **`customfield_24001`** (Folder → **`AI Generated `** when the instance uses that label) and **`customfield_29300`** (Test Requirement → **`STORY_KEY`**) on each key in **`meta.mcpCreatedKeys`**, so TM metadata matches manually fixed tickets (e.g. [EPMRPP-115879](https://jiraeu.epam.com/browse/EPMRPP-115879)) when MCP/LLM omit those fields.

### Linking Tests to the Story (required)

After creating or updating each Test issue, perform **both** of the following:

1. **Issue link — relation `is tested by` (Story → Test):** On the **Story** issue, linked Tests must appear under **is tested by**, **not** under **is a test for**. Those two phrases are the inward/outward labels of the **same** Jira link type on **`jiraeu.epam.com`**; wording depends on **which issue is `inwardIssue` vs `outwardIssue`** when the link is created.

   **EPMRPP (`jiraeu.epam.com`) — use this link type only for Story ↔ Test:**
   - **Link type name:** `QaSpace test`
   - **Link type id:** `12700` (REST: `/rest/api/2/issueLinkType/12700`)
   - **`jira_get_link_types`** with `name_filter: test` lists it with **`inward`:** `is a test for`, **`outward`:** `is tested by`.

   **REST / MCP create:** For type **`QaSpace test`**, set **`inwardIssue` = Story (`STORY_KEY`)** and **`outwardIssue` = Test** so that a **`jira_get_issue(STORY_KEY, fields=issuelinks)`** returns each Test under **`outward_issue`** (matches manually correct links on e.g. [EPMRPP-114990](https://jiraeu.epam.com/browse/EPMRPP-114990)). **Do not** swap keys—**`inwardIssue` = Test** and **`outwardIssue` = Story** makes the Story show **is a test for**.

   If your MCP names the tool **`jira_create_issue_link`** (or similar), pass the same type (`name` **`QaSpace test`** or `id` **`12700`**) and the same inward/outward issue keys. **Do not** use a different “Test” link type on this instance (e.g. type name **`Test`** / id **`10600`**) unless the team standard changes—verify with **`jira_get_issue`** on a correctly linked Story.
2. **Test Requirement (`STORY_KEY`):** Set **`customfield_29300`** (**Test Requirement** in the UI; Jira name **Test requirement**, TM type `requirement`—see **`jira_search_fields`** with **`keyword`:** `Test requirement`) to the **User Story** **`STORY_KEY`** (same key as the **QaSpace test** link and as git **`generated/jira-tests/<STORY_KEY>/`**). On [EPMRPP-115882](https://jiraeu.epam.com/browse/EPMRPP-115882) the field is present but unset (**`customfield_29300`** has an empty **`value`**). Mirror the **value shape** from any Test that already has a requirement (e.g. **`jira_get_issue(EPMRPP-115858, fields=customfield_29300)`**—story [EPMRPP-114988](https://jiraeu.epam.com/browse/EPMRPP-114988)) when calling **`jira_create_issue`** / **`jira_update_issue`**. **Do not** point **Test requirement** at a Sub-task key when **`STORY_KEY`** is the parent User Story.

Both steps apply to **newly created** and **updated** (existing) Test issues alike. If the MCP tool does not support one of these operations, try alternatives your MCP exposes; continue best-effort. **Do not** describe linking / **Test requirement** / MCP limitations in the **completion comment** on the **Test Design** Sub-task after tests are synced (**Test Design sub-task comment after successful test generation**); **never** put that narrative on **`STORY_KEY`**.

### Sync with existing Jira Tests (no duplicates)

Whenever test generation runs against a story that may already have **Test** issues.

1. **After** the **Pre-generation MCP gate** passes, **before** bulk **`jira_create_issue`**, discover Tests already **linked** to **`STORY_KEY`**: e.g. **`jira_get_issue(STORY_KEY)`** with **`issuelinks`** (links where the story is **is tested by** the Test, or equivalent names per instance: **Tests** / **is tested by** / **tested by** / **tests**), and/or **`jira_search`** / JQL your MCP supports to list **Test** issues tied to that story.
2. **Do not** create a second Test for the same logical case. Match existing issues to planned **`tests[]`** rows by **Jira Test Summary** ↔ **`tests[].summary`** (normalize for comparison: trim, case-insensitive). When a match exists, use **`jira_update_issue`** to refresh **summary**, **`priority`** (**Test priority**), **`customfield_19206`**, **`customfield_19207`**, **`customfield_24000`**, **`customfield_24001`**, **`customfield_29300`** (**Test Requirement** → **`STORY_KEY`**), **`labels`**, and any other fields you maintain—**do not** **`jira_create_issue`** again for that row.
3. Use **`jira_create_issue`** **only** for planned tests that have **no** matching linked Test; after creation apply both linking steps from **Linking Tests to the Story** (relation type `is tested by` + **`customfield_29300`**).
4. Do **not** assume an empty Jira side when re-running the pipeline; always **read linked Tests first**, then **update or add**.

## Cursor Agent CLI (headless)

- Run **`cursor-agent` / `agent`** **only** in **GitHub Actions** for this repo’s generate workflow (**`--trust`**, **`--approve-mcps`**, **`--force`**). **Do not** add scripts/docs that run the headless agent locally. **No** blocking questions. **Style:** **`.cursor/rules/jira-test-cases-epmrpp-style.mdc`**; **shape:** **`.cursor/skills/jira-story-test-cases-md/SKILL.md`**. MCP setup: **`docs/GITHUB_SECRETS.md`**, **`docs/JIRA_MCP_OPTIONS.md`**, **`npm run render-mcp`**.

## Always use **STORY_KEY** — verify first

- **CI:** **`ISSUE_KEY`** = dispatch target; **`STORY_KEY`** = workflow-resolved story (parent when target is Sub-task). If they **differ**, **`ISSUE_KEY`** is **trigger only**. Scope: **`jira_getIssue(STORY_KEY)`** only — description, summary (title context), AC/DoD fields. **`generated/jira-tests/<STORY_KEY>/`** and Test **links** use **`STORY_KEY`**; **`tests[].summary`** (test case **names**) must **not** contain **`STORY_KEY`** or the Sub-task **`ISSUE_KEY`** when they differ (**`.cursor/rules/jira-test-cases-epmrpp-style.mdc`**).
- **IDE:** User may paste a Sub-task. **`jira_getIssue`** → if Sub-task, **`STORY_KEY = parent.key`**, then fetch the story. Never use Sub-task **description**/**summary** for scenarios when the story is the parent.

## Pre-generation MCP gate (before any tests)

**Before** authoring tests or writing **`generated/jira-tests/<STORY_KEY>/tests.json`**, use **Jira MCP** to call **`jira_getIssue(STORY_KEY)`** (or equivalent) and load at least Jira **`summary`**, **`description`**, **`priority`**, **`issuetype`**, **`parent`**, and AC/DoD-style fields if available.

- **Gate passes** when: the MCP call **succeeds**; the Jira issue **`summary`** (the **issue title** in Jira—**not** the **`tests[].summary`** field you write in **`tests.json`**) is a **non-empty** string; **`description`** is **present** in the response (value may be null, empty, or empty ADF).
- **Only after the gate passes:** derive tests, write **`tests.json`**, sync Jira Tests (see **Sync with existing Jira Tests**), or apply **Empty story** (below) if description + AC are genuinely empty.

**Failed gate (MCP error, missing tool, auth/network failure, missing/empty Jira `summary`):** **CI must fail.** **Do not** write **`tests.json`** or **`meta.json`**. **`scripts/verify-mcp-jira.js`** exits non-zero when **`tests.json`** is missing under **`generated/jira-tests/<STORY_KEY>/`**, so GitHub Actions shows the job **failed** (red). **Never** use **`tests: []`** + empty **`meta.json`** to simulate success.

## Story-linked Confluence, Figma, and GitLab (MCP reads)

**After** the **Pre-generation MCP gate** passes and you have **`jira_getIssue(STORY_KEY)`** (or equivalent), **before** you finalize test coverage, check whether the story references **Confluence**, **Figma**, or **EPAM GitLab** (**`git.epam.com`**) by URL.

**Where to look:** Jira **`description`** (plain text or extract link targets from ADF if your tools support it), AC/DoD-style custom fields, and—if you fetch them via Jira MCP—**comments** on **`STORY_KEY`**.

### When Confluence links appear

- Typical signals: hostnames or paths for your Confluence instance (e.g. **`/wiki/`**, **`confluence.`**, org knowledge-base hosts), page links embedded in the description or AC.
- Use **Confluence** read/search tools from the **Atlassian MCP** server (**`atlassian`** in **`.cursor/mcp.json`**). Exact tool names depend on the server build—use whatever Confluence tools the session exposes (get page, search, etc.).
- **Read-only:** use MCP to pull content needed to understand acceptance criteria, flows, or copy **referenced by the link**. **Do not** invent details that exist only on the linked page without fetching it when the link is present and MCP is available.
- **Minimize calls:** Deduplicate URLs; **one** successful read per **distinct** page is enough—**do not** re-fetch the same page, run broad Confluence searches, or open linked child pages unless the story explicitly links to them.

### When Figma links appear

- Typical signals: **`figma.com`** URLs (e.g. **`/file/`**, **`/design/`**) including file key and, when present, node/frame identifiers.
- Use tools from the **Figma MCP** server (**`acuvity-mcp-server-figma`** in **`.cursor/mcp.json`** — **`docker.io/acuvity/mcp-server-figma`** via **`${CONTAINER_CMD}`** in CI). Use whatever read tools the session exposes so UI-oriented tests align with design intent (layout, labels, states) when the story points to a file or frame.
- **Minimize Figma API calls (Cursor / CI — reduces 429 rate limits):**
  - **Collect first:** Parse the story once; list **unique** file keys (and node ids if present). **Deduplicate** identical URLs.
  - **Prefer fewer, wider reads:** If a tool can return a **whole file** or **multiple nodes in one call**, use that instead of many small calls. **Do not** enumerate every frame or component “to be thorough.”
  - **One success per file key:** After a call returns usable data for a file, **do not** call Figma again for the same file key unless the first response was empty or clearly incomplete.
  - **No exploration:** **Do not** use Figma MCP to browse, search, or open files **not** linked from the story text.

### When GitLab (`git.epam.com`) links appear

- Typical signals: **`https://git.epam.com/`** URLs—e.g. **`/-/blob/`** links to requirement **Markdown** or other docs, merge requests, issues, or snippets embedded in the description or AC.
- Use tools from the **GitLab MCP** server (**`gitlab`** in **`.cursor/mcp.json`** — **`docker.io/mcp/gitlab:latest`** via **`${CONTAINER_CMD}`** in CI). Exact tool names depend on the server build—use whatever read tools the session exposes to retrieve **file or document content** (and minimal supporting metadata if required) for resources **referenced by the story link**.
- **Read-only:** pull content needed for acceptance criteria, flows, or copy **referenced by the link**. **Do not** invent details that exist only in the linked GitLab resource without fetching it when the link is present and MCP is available.
- **Minimize calls:** Deduplicate URLs; **one** successful read per **distinct** linked URL unless the first response is empty or clearly incomplete. **Do not** list entire repositories, walk unrelated directory trees, search broadly, or open projects/files **not** linked from the story (same spirit as Figma **no exploration**).

### If there are no such links

- **Do not** call Confluence, Figma, or GitLab MCP for exploration unrelated to URLs found on the story.

### If links exist but MCP read fails

- Optional context only: **do not** fail the whole run or treat this as a failed **Pre-generation MCP gate**. Complete tests from Jira text. **Do not** mention Confluence, Figma, or GitLab read failures in the **completion comment** on the **Test Design** Sub-task after tests are generated (**Test Design sub-task comment after successful test generation**); **do not** comment those on **`STORY_KEY`**. **Never** put tokens or secrets in **`generated/`** or repo files.
- **Streamed / assistant-visible output (CI log and IDE):** When a Confluence, Figma, or GitLab MCP call fails—**including HTTP 429**, rate limits, timeouts, or auth errors—**do not** narrate the failure in your reply. **Do not** quote status codes (**`429`**, **`403`**, etc.), provider error payloads, or hedging lines such as *“Figma returned 429; continuing from Jira only”* / *“Confluence unavailable; using Jira only”*. Proceed with the next useful step (e.g. Jira MCP) **without** announcing that you are falling back or why linked specs were skipped.

## Jira fetch required (not the same as empty story)

This section aligns with the **Pre-generation MCP gate** above.

- **Empty story** (below) applies **only** after **`jira_getIssue(STORY_KEY)`** **succeeds** (gate passed) and you have **actually read** the story’s **description** and AC/DoD-style fields from the response.
- If **Jira MCP is unavailable**, **`jira_getIssue`** **fails**, or the **gate** does not pass: **do not** treat that as an empty story. **Do not** write **`tests: []`** + **`meta.json`**. **Do not** produce a result that looks like a successful empty-story outcome.
- **CI:** Use **Generate Test Cases** on GitHub Actions (rendered **`.cursor/mcp.json`** + secrets) or **Cursor IDE** with working Jira MCP. If you cannot pass the gate, **omit** **`generated/jira-tests/<STORY_KEY>/tests.json`** so **`scripts/verify-mcp-jira.js`** fails; **never** substitute guesses or Sub-task text for the story body.

## Empty story — **do not** create tests

**No testable content** when **description** is empty (incl. empty ADF) **and** AC/DoD-style fields you fetched are empty—**after** the **Pre-generation MCP gate** passed (successful **`jira_getIssue(STORY_KEY)`**). **Jira `summary` alone** is not enough to invent scenarios when description + AC are empty.

Then: **`tests: []`**, **`meta.json`** with **`"jiraPublish": "mcp"`**, **`"mcpCreatedKeys": []`**. No **`jira_create_issue`** / **`jira_createIssue`**. No Sub-task backfill.

## Output directory

**Only** **`generated/jira-tests/<STORY_KEY>/`**. **`STORY_KEY`** = story used for requirements (in CI: parent when input was Sub-task).

## `tests.json`

```json
{
  "version": 1,
  "tests": [
    {
      "summary": "string (required)",
      "testSteps": "string (Preconditions + Steps as plain text for Jira Test Steps field)",
      "expectedResult": "string (maps to Expected result custom field)",
      "description": "optional Markdown"
    }
  ]
}
```

- **`summary`:** Plain EPMRPP title only—**do not** put **`STORY_KEY`** or (when it differs) Sub-task **`ISSUE_KEY`** in the text. Title shape: **`.cursor/rules/jira-test-cases-epmrpp-style.mdc`**.

## `meta.json`

After MCP **creates and/or updates** Tests **or** when **`tests`** is empty:

```json
{
  "jiraPublish": "mcp",
  "mcpCreatedKeys": ["PROJ-201", "PROJ-202"]
}
```

**`mcpCreatedKeys`:** same **length** and **order** as **`tests`** (use **`[]`** if **`tests`** is **`[]`**). Each entry is the Jira **Test issue key** for that **`tests[]`** row after sync—**updated** existing issues and **newly created** issues both count (the name **`mcpCreatedKeys`** is historical). **`scripts/verify-mcp-jira.js`** enforces length and valid keys in CI.

## Test Design sub-task comment after successful test generation

**Do not** add this completion summary comment on the **User Story** (**`STORY_KEY`**).

After **`tests.json`** and **`meta.json`** are written and Jira **Test** issues are synced for **`STORY_KEY`**, add **one** Jira **comment** (via Jira MCP) **only** on the **Test Design** **Sub-task**—the work item that tracks test design for that story, **not** on **`STORY_KEY`**.

- **GitHub Actions:** **`__ISSUE_KEY__`** is the workflow dispatch target. When **`__ISSUE_KEY__` ≠ `__STORY_KEY__`**, **`__ISSUE_KEY__`** is the **Test Design** Sub-task (**trigger only** for requirements); post the completion comment **only** on **`__ISSUE_KEY__`**. When **`__ISSUE_KEY__` = `__STORY_KEY__`** (dispatch from the story itself), **do not** add this comment on the story—**omit** the completion comment (prefer dispatching from the Test Design Sub-task).
- **IDE / manual:** Post **only** on the **Test Design** Sub-task the user or flow triggered from. If you have **`STORY_KEY`** but **no** Sub-task key for test design, **omit** the completion comment—**do not** use **`STORY_KEY`**.

**Include only:**

- A **short summary** line (e.g. how many Tests were created or updated, reference to **AI-generated** / **Generate Test Cases** run if helpful).
- A **list** of the **Test** work items: each line **Jira issue key** + **Test Summary** title (or markdown links `KEY — title`). Match **`mcpCreatedKeys`** / **`tests[].summary`**.

**Do not** include in that comment: **gaps**, **limitations**, **disclaimers**, partial failures, MCP/tool **could not**, missing coverage, linked specs (Confluence / Figma / GitLab) **could not be retrieved**, linking or **Test requirement** issues, “manual follow-up”, or any negative or hedging language. Keep the comment factual and positive—summary + list only.

## MCP servers (CI)

- On the runner: pull the images declared in **`.cursor/mcp.template.json`**, run **`node scripts/render-mcp-config.js`**, copy **`.cursor/mcp.json`** to **`~/.cursor/mcp.json`** so the Cursor CLI loads **Atlassian** (Jira + optional Confluence), **Figma** MCP (optional), and **GitLab** MCP (optional; **`gitlab`** / **`docker.io/mcp/gitlab:latest`** when **`GITLAB_*`** env is set)—workflow **Generate MCP config from template**.
- Prefer the **same Jira project** as the story unless requirements say otherwise.
- **Reads** for test design: **`jira_getIssue(STORY_KEY)`** for requirements; **plus** **Confluence** / **Figma** / **GitLab** MCP when the story contains links (see **Story-linked Confluence, Figma, and GitLab**); **plus** discovery of **linked Test** issues on that story (see **Sync with existing Jira Tests**) so reruns do not duplicate Tests.
- **Writes to Jira (Test issues):** Jira MCP only (**`jira_update_issue`** and **`jira_create_issue`** as appropriate); if linking is unsupported, use your team’s MCP-side approach. **Do not** use Confluence, Figma, or GitLab MCP to mutate external systems during test generation—**read** linked specs only.

## Safety

- **Never** put secrets or tokens under **`generated/`** or in repo files.
